Here is the input problem:
  Axiom 1 (eqNat_1): eqNat(zero, zero) = true.
  Axiom 2 (eqNat_2): eqNat(zero, suc(X)) = false.
  Axiom 3 (eqNat_3): eqNat(suc(X), zero) = false.
  Axiom 4 (eqNat_4): eqNat(suc(X), suc(Y)) = eqNat(X, Y).
  Axiom 5 (app_fn_id_1): app(fn_id, X) = X.
  Axiom 6 (app_fn_const_1): app(fn_const(X), Y) = X.
  Axiom 7 (app_fn_case_Nat_1): app(fn_case_Nat(X, Y), zero) = X.
  Axiom 8 (app_fn_case_Nat_2): app(fn_case_Nat(X, Y), suc(Z)) = app(Y, Z).
  Axiom 9 (prop_twice_1): prop_twice(X, Y) = eqNat(app(X, app(X, Y)), app(X, Y)).
  Axiom 10 (reflexivity): equals(X, X) = true.
  Axiom 11 (prop_twice): equals(prop_twice(X, Y), false) = false.
  Goal 1 (true_equals_false): true = false.

1. eqNat(zero, zero) -> true
2. eqNat(zero, suc(X)) -> false
3. eqNat(suc(X), zero) -> false
4. eqNat(suc(X), suc(Y)) -> eqNat(X, Y)
5. app(fn_id, X) -> X
6. app(fn_const(X), Y) -> X
7. app(fn_case_Nat(X, Y), zero) -> X
8. app(fn_case_Nat(X, Y), suc(Z)) -> app(Y, Z)
9. eqNat(app(X, app(X, Y)), app(X, Y)) -> prop_twice(X, Y)
10. equals(X, X) -> true
11. equals(prop_twice(X, Y), false) -> false
12. eqNat(X, X) -> prop_twice(fn_id, X)
13. prop_twice(fn_id, zero) -> true
14. equals(true, false) -> false
15. prop_twice(fn_const(X), Y) -> prop_twice(fn_id, X)
16. prop_twice(fn_id, suc(X)) -> prop_twice(fn_id, X)
17. eqNat(app(fn_case_Nat(X, Y), X), X) -> prop_twice(fn_case_Nat(X, Y), zero)
18. prop_twice(fn_case_Nat(zero, X), zero) -> true
19. eqNat(app(X, Y), suc(Y)) -> prop_twice(fn_case_Nat(suc(Y), X), zero)
20. prop_twice(fn_case_Nat(suc(X), fn_id), zero) = eqNat(X, suc(X))
21. equals(eqNat(X, suc(X)), false) -> false
22. false -> true

The conjecture is true! Here is a proof.

Axiom 1 (eqNat_2): eqNat(zero, suc(X)) = false.
Axiom 2 (app_fn_id_1): app(fn_id, X) = X.
Axiom 3 (app_fn_case_Nat_1): app(fn_case_Nat(X, Y), zero) = X.
Axiom 4 (app_fn_case_Nat_2): app(fn_case_Nat(X, Y), suc(Z)) = app(Y, Z).
Axiom 5 (prop_twice_1): prop_twice(X, Y) = eqNat(app(X, app(X, Y)), app(X, Y)).

Goal 1 (prop_twice): prop_twice(X, Y) = false.
The goal is true when:
  X = fn_case_Nat(suc(zero), fn_id)
  Y = zero

Proof:
  prop_twice(fn_case_Nat(suc(zero), fn_id), zero)
= { by axiom 5 (prop_twice_1) }
  eqNat(app(fn_case_Nat(suc(zero), fn_id), app(fn_case_Nat(suc(zero), fn_id), zero)), app(fn_case_Nat(suc(zero), fn_id), zero))
= { by axiom 3 (app_fn_case_Nat_1) }
  eqNat(app(fn_case_Nat(suc(zero), fn_id), suc(zero)), app(fn_case_Nat(suc(zero), fn_id), zero))
= { by axiom 3 (app_fn_case_Nat_1) }
  eqNat(app(fn_case_Nat(suc(zero), fn_id), suc(zero)), suc(zero))
= { by axiom 4 (app_fn_case_Nat_2) }
  eqNat(app(fn_id, zero), suc(zero))
= { by axiom 2 (app_fn_id_1) }
  eqNat(zero, suc(zero))
= { by axiom 1 (eqNat_2) }
  false

RESULT: Theorem (the conjecture is true).
